.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt OPENMAIL.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openmail.conf
.Nd OpenMail system configuration
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the configuration format used by
.Xr openmail 8 .
The default file is
.Pa /etc/openmail/config.toml ;
.Fl f
selects another file.
.Pp
The file uses TOML syntax.
Unknown keys, duplicate keys, malformed values, and incomplete Maildir
configuration are errors.
The file must exist, be a regular file, and contain at most 64 KiB of UTF-8 text.
An empty file selects the default settings.
.Pp
Keep system settings under
.Pa /etc/openmail ,
owned by root and readable by the service account.
Mode 0750 for the directory and 0640 for the file are suitable when the
service group has read access.
Keep mail and writable SQLite state outside the configuration directory.
.Ss Global settings
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic http_listen No = Ar address
HTTP listen address as a quoted IP address and port.
The default is
.Qq 127.0.0.1:8080 .
Only loopback IP addresses and nonzero ports are accepted.
IPv6 loopback, for example
.Qq [::1]:8080 ,
is supported.
Hostnames and wildcard addresses are not accepted.
Terminate public HTTPS at
.Xr relayd 8
and forward to this local backend.
.El
.Ss Maildir settings
The optional
.Ic [maildir]
table enables configuration for explicit
.Fl -scan
operation.
It is not polled by the HTTP service yet.
Both settings are required when the table is present:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic root No = Ar path
Absolute path to an existing Maildir with
.Pa tmp ,
.Pa new ,
and
.Pa cur
directories.
.It Ic database No = Ar path
Absolute path to the private SQLite metadata database.
Its parent directory must exist and the database must be outside the
Maildir tree and system configuration directory.
Use a dedicated private directory.
New database files are created with mode 0600.
Existing permissions remain the operator's responsibility.
.El
.Pp
Maildir filenames must be UTF-8.
Messages larger than 64 MiB, ambiguous message keys, and unreadable or
incomplete mailbox structures cause the scan to fail.
Message files and traversed mailbox directories must not be symbolic links.
.Pp
The database is bound to one canonical Maildir root.
A different root, unrelated database, or unsupported schema version is rejected.
SQLite stores IDs, locators, flags, content fingerprints, and change records;
original message content remains in Maildir.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/openmail/
System settings directory.
.It Pa /etc/openmail/config.toml
Required default configuration file.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Default local HTTP service with a Maildir for explicit scans:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
http_listen = "127.0.0.1:8080"

[maildir]
root = "/var/mail/alice/Maildir"
database = "/var/db/openmail/alice/index.sqlite"
.Ed
.Pp
Validate without opening mail or creating a database:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openmail -n -f /etc/openmail/config.toml
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openmail 8
